Fetched 2026-09-12. Apache-2.0, Mozilla.

Vendored rather than loaded from a CDN for the same reason the sql.js
worker next door is: this site ships static files with no build step and
no third-party script tags, so a page cannot start depending on someone
else's uptime or start reporting its readers to them.

That matters more here than anywhere else on the site. This library
reads the CV a person picks, and it runs entirely in their browser: the
file is never uploaded, and the only thing that ever reaches us is the
list of skills they choose to save. Loading the parser from a CDN would
have told that CDN, on every analysis, that somebody was parsing a
document on this domain.

Unmodified. pdf.worker.min.mjs must sit next to pdf.min.mjs; account.js
points workerSrc at it explicitly rather than relying on the default
resolution, which assumes a bundler.
